      {
        "atom_id": "atom::c2466fcd955a9bec6b8ae2db",
        "source_handle": "P0354",
        "field_path": [
          "study_summary_A",
          "approach"
        ],
        "value": "The authors performed a meta-analysis of raw 16S rRNA amplicon and whole-genome shotgun (WGS) metagenomic sequencing data from five public datasets (Chaput, Frankel, Gopalakrishnan, Matson, Routy). They applied a uniform bioinformatics pipeline: Resphera Insight for 16S taxonomic assignment and MetaPhlAn2 for WGS. Statistical analysis included random effects meta-analysis models (Hedges' g) to identify species enriched in R or NR groups, correcting for false discovery rate (FDR). An 'integrated microbiome prediction index' was constructed using weighted coefficients of significant species. Validation was performed on three independent cohorts (Peters, Hakozaki, Zheng) representing melanoma, NSCLC, and hepatocellular carcinoma (HCC). Sensitivity/specificity analyses (AUC) were used to evaluate index performance.",
        "role": "evidence",
        "snapshot_ids": [
          "snapshot::a7a7de9fbd4946fc2daa9ddf"
        ]
      },
      {
